  "body": "**Stacked on #1131** (M5's #541, sinker burn to depth, branch `issue/541-sinker-burn-depth`). Retarget to `main` before #1131 merges. Fork synced at v0.18.0 (process files at PROCESS_VERSION 17).\n\n## What changed\n\nA Sinker Burn can now **orbit at the burn floor** after the plunge. The orbit is circular, vector or planetary, and it is expanded into explicit Feed chords (#290 D3), so the 3-axis stock sim's box atom (#541) verifies every move that would post. Corner joins are included, under the same laws as #541's burns.\n\n- `motion::sinker_orbit` (new) holds the pattern geometry.\n  - circular: out along +X to the radius, then one full circle;\n  - vector: out to the radius and back along N evenly spaced directions from +X;\n  - planetary: an Archimedean spiral from 0 to the radius over N turns, closed by a full circle.\n  - Every vertex is on or inside the stated radius (an ulp-past rounding is pulled back in), so no chord overshoots it. Chords keep a sagitta of 0.001 mm or less. Their count is a multiple of 4, so the ±X/±Y directions are vertices and a rectangular electrode's walls move out by exactly the radius. The counts are bounded (vectors 1..=72, turns 1..=20), so an orbit cannot balloon into a hang.\n- `motion::sinker::burn_to_depth` runs the orbit at the tip Z at the servo feed and returns to the centre before the rapid retract. With `orbit: None` the plain plunge's CL and params digest are unchanged.\n- `SinkerBurnOp.orbit: Option<SinkerOrbit>` is an additive field and file key (`orbit: { kind, radius, vectors, turns }`), so old files load. It is edited through `CreateOperation` / `EditOperationParams`. MCP reaches it through the existing params JSON door (`add_operation` / `edit_operation`, `\"orbit\": null` drops it). There is no new command, so there is no new MCP tool. The minimal sinker page gets Orbit / radius / vectors / turns rows on Passes.\n- **Machine law** (`sinker_op::orbit_law`, #290 D6), refused by name at generation:\n  - `machine X lists no vector orbit under edm.orbits ...`\n  - `machine X states no maximum orbit radius (edm.max_orbit_radius) ...` (absent is not unlimited)\n  - `the circular orbit radius 0.600 exceeds machine X's maximum orbit radius 0.500`\n  - The job and the staleness stamp read it through `burn_gap`, so a re-stated orbit list or maximum marks the op stale. A garbled orbit is refused at the door (`is_sane`).\n- **No schema change.** `edm.orbits[]` and `edm.max_orbit_radius` already exist in the `.mch` edm section from #530 (on this base), and #1141's post reads the same fields. They are read as they are. This PR emits no `EdmOrbit` PARAM: the orbit posts as its explicit moves, and a canned word on top would be a double orbit (D3's later item).\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/544-sinker-orbits.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `crates/app/tests/sinker_orbit.rs` (new, 6 tests):\n  - `sinker_orbit_circular_matches_golden`: golden `tests/golden/sinker_orbit_circular.cl`, which I read. It has the plunge to Z 14.050, out to +0.200 X, 32 CCW chords on the r = 0.2 circle back to +X, a return to the centre, and the retract. Max excursion is 0.200.\n  - `a_circular_orbit_widens_the_simulated_cavity_by_its_radius`: on the simulated stock (0.05 cell), the cavity floor reaches electrode + gap + radius on ±X and ±Y, and the next column out stands untouched. The same burn without the orbit stops one radius short. The furthest move is the radius exactly.\n  - `every_orbit_pattern_stays_in_its_radius_and_verifies_clean`: all three patterns stay inside the radius with chords only, and `simulate_document` finds 0 gouge cells in the orbit-sized cavity.\n  - `an_orbit_wider_than_the_parts_cavity_is_convicted_by_the_stock_sim`\n  - `an_unlisted_pattern_and_an_over_radius_orbit_are_refused_by_name`: also covers the unstated maximum (refused), radius == max (admitted), and the garbled-orbit door.\n  - `the_orbit_round_trips_the_file_and_rides_the_mcp_params_door`: file round trip, MCP add, an over-max edit refused at generate, undo, an unlisted pattern refused, `orbit: null` back to a plunge.\n- `motion::sinker_orbit` unit tests: every pattern for radii 0.0005..12 is inside its radius and closes on the centre; the chord tolerance holds and the axis directions are vertices; garbled numbers are refused by name.\n- `sinker_burn.rs` (#541) is unchanged apart from `orbit: None` in its literals, and its golden is byte-identical.\n- Gate: the full `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head `49904407` ran tools, post, sim, motion, app and ui: 3437 passed, 1 failed. The failure is `coarse_laws::every_kind_is_either_judged_or_refused_for_a_stated_reason_on_a_reduced_model` (\"SinkerBurn is judged while a tolerance is left\"). It is **pre-existing on the #1131 base**: I reproduced it on the base tree without this commit. `fidelity_law.rs` refuses `Section::Sinker`, but the test's `refused` list has no `SinkerBurn`. This PR touches neither file. It belongs to #1131.\n- The sinker suites (`sinker_burn`, `sinker_orbit`), `edm_machine`, `edm_conditions`, `golden_cl` and `project_roundtrip` are green. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- **Not exercised on a real EDM control.** The fixtures are synthetic: an invented condition, invented orbit words and an invented 0.5 mm maximum.\n- Posting waits on #542 (#1141). That post refuses arcs, and how it treats the lateral orbit chords has not been checked here. The post script is untouched.\n- The stock view / playback (field eye) still refuses an electrode by name (#541), so the orbit is judged by the program verdict's column engine only.\n- The minimal sinker page gains orbit rows; #548's full pages (PR #1165) will need them carried over.\n- Interaction with #543's undersize (PR #1136) and #546's wear compensation was not exercised. Both touch the same op, and whichever merges second may need a small merge.\n\nChangelog: Sinker Burn orbits (circular, vector, planetary) at the burn floor, expanded into explicit moves the stock sim verifies; a pattern the machine does not list, or a radius past its stated maximum, is refused by name (#544, PR #1166)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #544\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
